five, six years, but eventually I go out and test the waters. I think what happens is the fear of failing gets overtaken by the fear of failing to try. And so if you have a great surgeon or you believe that a film you're making is going to change the world, then at some point you shift from worrying about regretting, making a fool of yourself, to regretting, never taking a chance. And as you know, that's what psychologists consistently find about regret, that a lot of people are afraid in the moment of taking the risk, but that in the long run our biggest regrets are in actions, the chances we didn't take.
